# The NREOCRC synthetic corpus is an immutable test fixture whose SHA-256
# hashes are recorded in tests/fixtures/nreocrc/manifest.json as part of the
# corpus's own provenance guarantee (Prompt 13). Line-ending normalization
# on checkout (core.autocrlf) would silently change these files' bytes on
# some machines and break that guarantee - `-text` disables any such
# conversion, so the files are always checked out exactly as committed.
tests/fixtures/nreocrc/immutable_original/** -text

# CLAUDE-P40-VW7A-QA: vendored, third-party PDF.js distribution files
# (static/js/vendor/pdfjs/README.md has the exact source/version) - must
# stay byte-identical to what was actually downloaded and verified, the
# same "line-ending normalization would silently change bytes" reasoning
# as the NREOCRC corpus above, not re-derived.
static/js/vendor/pdfjs/*.mjs -text
